activitytrack-desktop (1.0.0~alfa-1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ALPHA pre-release of 1.0 (tag v1.0.0-alfa-1). Synchronisation requires the
    server and every device to be on 1.0 (wire schema 3: older apps are told
    to update). Existing data is migrated automatically and backups made by
    older versions can still be restored.
  * The to-do is no longer a separate object: it is an activity in the state
    "Da fare", one activity from plan to closure. Displayed states have an
    icon and a colour; there is no "Sospendi" (an activity becomes Sospesa
    only when another one starts). Priorities are named (Nessuna ... Emergenza)
    and "Ignorate" is replaced by the Cestino (Ripristina / Elimina
    definitivamente). Absences have a kind (Assenza, Ferie, Permesso,
    Malattia), an optional company and one segment per working day.
  * Home header and empty card with four buttons (Da fare, Lavoro, Viaggio,
    Assenza); Viaggio starts at once; Gia iniziata and Passata modes; absence
    dialog; detail with state pill, total and actions; the tray has no
    Sospendi and the stop sheet is gone. Built on the library 1.0.0~alfa-1.

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:31:24 +0000

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.9.9, on the library 0.9.9, in step with ActivityTrack 0.9.9:
    Settings, General, Updates asks the paired server for a newer version (a
    signed manifest, checked against the key of the pairing link), notifies
    once per version and downloads the package with its sha256 checked, never
    for an installation of the package manager; the Scarica button is off
    while a download runs.

