activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta5-1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The look and the use of the phone's app: Material 3 light or dark as
    the system, the Home's big card with round buttons and small cards,
    the list with state marks, filter chips, a rail with Home, Da fare
    and Impostazioni.
  * Keyboard shortcuts in the window (Ctrl+N, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+T, Ctrl+D,
    Ctrl+F, Ctrl+1..3, F5) and system-wide ones (Ctrl+Alt+A start,
    Ctrl+Alt+P pause/resume, Ctrl+Alt+S stop), configurable: Windows,
    X11 (python3-xlib), Wayland through the desktop portal (python3-jeepney);
    and --start, --pause, --stop for the desktop's own shortcuts.
  * Fix: the sync worker no longer closes the store after each run, which
    with python3-activitytrack 0.9.4-beta5 closed the window's connection
    and stopped the application after the first sync.

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:16:29 +0100

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security review fixes: the single-instance socket in the user's
    runtime folder; closing the window without a tray quits once; quitting
    during a blocked sync takes at most 2 s; pairing cannot be cancelled
    half-way; update links only to github.com; postpone label as the action.
  * On the library 0.9.4-beta5 (its security fixes).

